			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@stefan\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>stefan</span></a></span> Fwiw, here it is (sparkly-text with Shadow DOM)</p><p><a href=\"https://codepen.io/tbroyer/pen/abXgYEy\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">codepen.io/tbroyer/pen/abXgYEy</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p><p>It won't work in Safari &lt; 16.4 due to lack of support for constructible stylesheet (I used the same detection code as Zach) but that can be worked around if needed by adding a &lt;style&gt; element in the shadow DOM.<br>BTW, things could be optimized too (create CSSStyleSheet once only, clone the sparkle rather than innerHTML every single time)</p><p>(I also added the CSS pointer-events like in Zach's snow-fall)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
